WEBVTT

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.140
Can you imagine...

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:41.350
...a life in which you could never
touch the one you love?

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:44.230
He takes the life of whatever he touches.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:47.690
That was the curse the witch put on him.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:51.990
Plants, animals... and people
are no exception, of course.

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:55.370
Regarding her son, doomed to live his life
without knowing the warmth of another,

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:58.080
his mother only complained.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.580
"That child is like Death incarnate..."

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:01.580
she said.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:08.590
You're getting too close to me
again today, Alice! Way too close!

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:11.300
Your reactions are so adorable,
Your Grace,

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.840
I can't help wanting to see them up close.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.890
Okay then, take this!

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:18.520
I won't get self-conscious
if I can't see you!

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.560
You truly are adorable, Your Grace.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.310
My ears are totally defenseless!

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:58.440
Episode 2 

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:59.580
Please forgive me for my extended absence.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:02.410
I have fully recovered
from my back injury,

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:05.580
so I shall be returning
to work as of today.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.420
That's wonderful.
Good to have you back, Rob.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:11.170
I imagine I caused you
some trouble as well, Alice.

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:14.380
I left the care of His Grace
entirely in your hands.

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:16.550
You needn't worry about me.

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:19.550
I was able to spend the night
together with His Grace, so...

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:22.100
Stop saying things that
could be misconstrued!

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:25.730
Seeing you two always
puts a smile on my face.

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:28.310
You need to keep your subordinate
from sexually harassing me!

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:34.400
And now, I shall take my leave.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.030
It's the morning after Rob got back,

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:42.790
and it looks like he's already
hard at work around the estate.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:46.460
Yes, even doing the jobs that
are too much for me to handle.

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:48.370
He's superhuman. That's why.

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:54.380
Rob's been a butler to me from the
time I lived at my family's residence.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.840
He was also the only one
to come with me to this estate.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.430
You could say he was like a father to me.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:08.140
So, how long do you plan
on standing there?

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:11.940
Rob has taken all the work
I would normally do.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:14.860
Does my presence here bother you?

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:17.320
Well, it's just that I can't
concentrate on my reading...

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:22.570
I hope I'm not disturbing you.
I've brought you your tea.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:24.540
But he was just in the yard a moment ago!

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:30.250
Aren't you working a bit too hard, Rob?

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:31.380
Who, me?

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:34.170
Well, you are sort of on the mend and all.

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:36.840
Why don't you let Alice
do some of the work, too?

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:40.050
How kind of you to worry.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:44.600
I may have been a bit too eager to get
back to work after my absence, but...

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:47.980
...you needn't worry about me, Your Grace.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:51.400
Very well. We'll divide the cleaning to be
done around the estate and get to work.

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:53.610
Let's go, Alice.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:54.610
All right.

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:03.620
What is with her?

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:07.080
This is really good!

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:11.170
Rob's work hasn't
suffered any, to be sure.

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:14.290
It may be boorish of me to worry.

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:15.210
Still...

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:16.380
Alice?

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:19.920
There's something I wanted to ask you...

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:24.140
I-It's me! What the heck
are you doing, Rob?

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:26.100
Oh, it's you, Your Grace.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:30.180
Forgive me. My eyes have been blurry
lately, and it makes things hard to see.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.310
That's a sign of aging eyes!

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:33.980
I've told you before, haven't I?

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:36.480
That lately, the effects of your
old age have gotten a bit worse.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.320
If you touch me, you'll die.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:40.860
That doesn't mean I want
you to avoid me, but...

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:43.570
...you have to look out
for yourself a bit more.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:45.200
And you're hard of hearing, too!

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:46.620
What's the matter?

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:50.250
Oh, Alice, it's you.
Can you talk some sense into him?

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:51.500
Pardon me.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:00.210
This is the real Alice, right?

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.970
It's Alice! She's the only
other person around here!

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:06.260
I don't get it.
Your work is flawless, and yet...

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:13.390
When you've been a butler for as long as
I have, your body remembers the work.

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:16.190
So, you needn't worry about me.

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:20.730
I shall serve you for as long
as I live, Your Grace.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:23.900
Rob...

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:26.950
Is it your back again?

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:28.830
So it seems...

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:47.970
All right. This is sounding good.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:51.310
In case my family decides to disown
me somewhere down the road,

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:56.270
I've been writing a bunch of songs
so I can make a living with my music.

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:59.310
For as long as I can remember,
the only thing I ever got praised for...

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:01.780
...was my piano playing.

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:05.070
Having still not found any way
of breaking the witch's curse,

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:09.700
playing the piano is my dream
as well as my only hope.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:11.240
Is that a requiem?

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:17.420
Forgive me. While I was cleaning, I heard
this beautiful song being played, and...

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:20.840
In that case, could you come up and
speak to me more like a normal person?

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:22.460
What do you mean by "normal"?

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:24.720
I mean, "Don't lean in so close to me"!

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:26.260
Don't bug me, okay?

00:07:26.260 --> 00:07:29.430
Rob is resting, so just do your own work.

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:30.890
Very well.

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:44.570
It's not like...

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:49.030
...I'm giving into...

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:53.540
...my baser emotions or anything...

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:58.460
Your Grace,

00:07:58.460 --> 00:07:59.790
you're staring too hard.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:02.170
I bet you were doing it on purpose!

00:08:02.170 --> 00:08:04.800
Since I can't concentrate,
save the cleaning for later and...

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:08.180
...come sit here and listen
to me play until I'm done.

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:09.260
All right.

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:11.600
Looks like I've got a front-row seat.

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:13.720
I wouldn't go so far as to say that.

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:25.670
It's a somber yet very beautiful song.

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:27.590
You know what?

00:09:27.590 --> 00:09:31.090
You told me it sounded
like a requiem earlier,

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:35.180
but I actually composed it
as a ballad for you.

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:38.060
I almost didn't ask you because
I was too embarrassed to,

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:42.390
but after thinking about it some more,
I really wanted you to hear it with me.

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:49.900
I'm feeling a bit tired,
so I think I'll take a nap.

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:53.200
Wake me up when dinner's ready.

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:57.790
I see. Very well...

00:10:00.790 --> 00:10:02.960
...I shall kiss you good night.

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:14.890
I was only kidding. If you're going
to take a nap, please do it in bed.

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:19.890
Well, that sure woke me up!

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:26.650
May I please be excused?

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:29.860
You barely touched your plate.

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:34.570
I'm on a diet. Please give me
a smaller helping tomorrow.

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:39.410
Hey, I'm starving. Don't we have
any apple crumble or something?

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:41.500
Didn't you say you were on a diet?

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:43.460
Come on, who cares?

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:49.800
Oh, that's right! I'm going out tomorrow,
so get the carriage ready.

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:05.770
It's so peaceful...

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:07.480
I'm making really good progress.

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:09.480
Looks like I'll get
more done than I planned.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:14.780
Oh, this mansion's as depressing as ever!

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:17.200
For being so run-down,
it's ridiculously huge!

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:19.910
The stress of just being here
would make me break out in zits!

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:21.160
Definitely bad for the skin!

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:24.290
I don't know how he manages to live here!

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:26.370
Oh, there you are!
I'm so sorry.

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:29.210
You're so unobtrusive I didn't
even notice you were there!

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:32.250
How long has it been, Dearest Brother?

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:34.670
Alice! Alice, come quick!

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:38.340
What's the matter?

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:41.600
You let her in the house again
without my permission, didn't you?

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:44.180
What a rude thing to say!

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:47.900
Lady Viola is Your Grace's
younger sister, so...

00:11:47.900 --> 00:11:49.060
That's right.

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:53.860
I have so graciously come to visit you,
so why don't you act happier?

00:11:53.860 --> 00:11:57.240
It seems my dearest brother
wishes to speak with me,

00:11:57.240 --> 00:11:58.530
so wait for me in the garden.

00:11:58.530 --> 00:11:59.780
Yes, milady.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.490
Nobody asked for this!

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:08.670
Mmm! This is great!

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:11.630
Tea is best served with
sweet crumpets, don't you think?

00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:14.760
I don't think I could ever get my fill.

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:16.760
When are you planning on leaving today?

00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:18.260
Oh, my God! How rude!

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:20.550
You don't have to tell me to go.
I'm not staying long.

00:12:22.180 --> 00:12:26.640
Mother will be angry with me
if she finds out I'm here.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:29.390
Hey, can I have some more sweets?

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:32.610
And some Assam tea brewed
with dried fruits, too!

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:33.980
Very well.

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:35.820
You've really got a lot of nerve!

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:43.490
My sister loves girly things like sweets
and talking about her love interests.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:48.660
I suspect she drops by occasionally
for a little change of pace.

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:50.250
But...

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:51.960
Hey, what are you looking at?

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:56.420
So, not only are you gloomy and unpopular,
you're also into very young girls?

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:59.550
...I just can't handle her
"charming" personality.

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:02.010
I brought you some sticky toffee pudding.

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:03.800
Wow! It looks delectable!

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:05.890
Sorry to put you to all this trouble.

00:13:05.890 --> 00:13:07.720
It was no trouble at all.

00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:16.440
Say, are you fond of that maid,
Dearest Brother?

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:17.570
Huh?!

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:22.450
Um... I'm fond of her...
I mean, I adore her...

00:13:22.450 --> 00:13:24.320
That was painful to watch.

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:26.450
Hey, that hurts!

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:28.660
Well, that explains it.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:30.660
My dearest brother's in love.

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:31.750
Oh, well.

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:35.590
Little Miss Viola here will just have to
make you popular, starting with that maid.

00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:38.170
Using "The Viola Method of
Instruction in the Art of Love."

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:39.510
The Viola Method?!

00:13:39.510 --> 00:13:43.720
For example, everybody's got a
complex about something, right?

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:47.220
All you've got to do is
just hide whatever it is.

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:50.480
I have a round face,
so I hide the contours.

00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:52.690
And it melts everyone's heart.

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:54.350
See? Look how adorable I am!

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:56.400
Sounds like you're tooting
your own horn a bit too much.

00:13:56.400 --> 00:14:01.240
In your case, Dearest Brother, you should
hide those dark circles under your eyes.

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:03.110
Y-You think?

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:03.780
Like this?

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:06.030
Eww! Pull it down some more.

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:07.160
Is this far enough?

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:09.040
I feared as much. You just don't have
what it takes to be a ladies' man.

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:10.580
Try again in the next life!

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:12.370
You sure do give up easily!

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:18.340
After all this chit-chatting with
Dearest Brother, it's gotten so late.

00:14:18.340 --> 00:14:20.260
Well, I was able to eat some tasty treats,

00:14:20.260 --> 00:14:23.430
so I guess it wasn't a total waste
of time. I'll come again sometime.

00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:25.890
Just stop dropping by unannounced, okay?

00:14:25.890 --> 00:14:26.850
Or better yet...

00:14:26.850 --> 00:14:30.140
Hurry up and break that curse so
you can come back and live with us.

00:14:31.060 --> 00:14:32.980
What are you blushing for?

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:36.400
If you think I said that out of concern
for you, then you are sorely mistaken.

00:14:36.400 --> 00:14:38.270
Who do you think you are, anyway?

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:40.280
You sure talk a lot of trash
on your way out...

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.900
Hey, what's the big idea--

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:45.570
Rob?!

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:49.160
Well, if it isn't Lady Viola!

00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:53.000
Oh, um... H-H-How long has it been?

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:54.500
It's been ages.

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:58.290
I see you made a special trip all
the way out here just to pay us a visit.

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:02.210
I, um... wanted to see you, so...

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:06.590
Oh, you better be careful,
or your hair will get in your eyes.

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:10.720
Seems the Viola Method
is totally ineffective...

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:13.270
Who'd have thought she
was into very old men...

00:15:21.110 --> 00:15:23.530
"Hurry up and break that curse," huh?

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:25.530
That's easy for her to say...

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:36.920
Alice! Alice, come quick!

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:40.750
What's the matter, Your Grace?

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:44.210
Why, it's a cat!

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:46.630
It must've wandered
in here from the forest.

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:49.340
I can't go into the piano room
as long as it's here.

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:51.720
Hurry up and shoo it out of here!

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:56.810
You truly are adorable, Your Grace,
to make such a fuss over a single cat.

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:59.440
I-It's not like I'm scared
of it or anything!

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:01.480
It's just that it's hard to
tell what animals will do,

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:04.190
so I get worried I might
accidentally touch them.

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:07.740
Here, kitty!

00:16:17.210 --> 00:16:18.460
Did you hear me?

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:19.790
Yes, I heard you.

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:23.960
But I just love animals.
They're so adorable.

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:28.470
It has a collar.
Could it be a house cat?

00:16:28.470 --> 00:16:31.100
Yeah, you're right. I wonder
if it ran away from home.

00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:33.390
Let's set it loose in
the forest right away.

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:35.970
Wait a...

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:40.650
Why is it after me?!

00:16:40.650 --> 00:16:42.650
Try not to fall, now!

00:16:42.650 --> 00:16:44.110
What?! Come save me!

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:45.440
Huh? Your Grace...

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:47.490
You mustn't crawl around
on your hands and knees!

00:16:47.490 --> 00:16:49.070
You think that looks like me?!

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:51.660
What you've got is worse
than a case of aging eyes!

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:55.580
I picked you up without thinking, but--
Hey! This feels like a cat!

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:56.750
Oh, how cute!

00:16:56.750 --> 00:16:58.460
Don't get all friendly with it!

00:16:58.460 --> 00:17:00.210
Run free, kitty cat!

00:17:00.210 --> 00:17:02.130
And after you went to
the trouble of catching it!

00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:07.130
Your Grace, the cat tore up
my clothes with its claws...

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:09.220
Is that something you've
got to tell me right now?!

00:17:09.220 --> 00:17:11.890
But I can sew this up, and it'll be fine.

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:14.050
You don't have to widen
the rips with your fingers!

00:17:20.230 --> 00:17:23.060
So, it was reacting to my bolo tie.

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:25.190
What a pesky cat!

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:29.110
It certainly is a drawback not
knowing what animals will do.

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:31.780
That includes you, too.
Stop fiddling with those rips!

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:34.450
What's this?

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:36.450
Your Grace, there's a note.

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:39.830
Could this be the cat's name?

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:40.830
Beats me.

00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:45.630
Please forgive me...

00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:47.170
What does this mean?

00:18:01.980 --> 00:18:05.730
So, you didn't run away.
You were abandoned. Just like me.

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:10.320
It's hard... being cast aside.

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:22.870
Well, it looks like the cat
already found a new family.

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:25.250
Your tea is ready.

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:29.760
Please come in soon, Your Grace.
You wouldn't want to catch a cold.

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:31.840
All right, I'm coming.

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:52.400
<i>In the gloom of the forest</i>

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:56.700
<i>I stand where I was abandoned</i>

00:18:56.700 --> 00:19:00.410
<i>No one will hear</i>

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:04.540
<i>My feeble, heart-rending cry</i>

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:08.710
<i>I want to go back</i>

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:12.710
<i>But I can never go back</i>

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:20.560
<i>To that warm and loving place</i>
<i>that I miss so much</i>

00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:24.520
So, this is where you've been, Your Grace.

00:19:24.520 --> 00:19:27.230
Your dinner is ready.

00:19:27.230 --> 00:19:30.110
What have you been doing?

00:19:30.110 --> 00:19:34.700
The moon is so beautiful, so I was
just standing here thinking.

00:19:34.700 --> 00:19:40.030
I don't come in here much, but the view
from this ballroom certainly is lovely.

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:42.290
No one comes in here much
because there's no reason to.

00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:44.200
Rob once told me that a long time ago,

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:47.960
my grandfather couldn't
dance to save his life,

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:51.170
so he used to come here
late at night to practice.

00:19:51.170 --> 00:19:55.720
And apparently, his dance partner
at the time was your mother.

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:01.140
Don't you find that interesting?

00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:06.690
My grandfather and your mother
danced in this very room.

00:20:06.690 --> 00:20:09.480
I feel like it was fate
that brought us here.

00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:12.610
It certainly could be an act of fate.

00:20:16.070 --> 00:20:20.370
S-Shall we give it a try ourselves?

00:20:20.370 --> 00:20:24.790
I can't touch you, but we can coordinate
our movements to approximate dancing.

00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:26.870
I must decline.

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:31.130
Oh, I see... I thought it
would be fun, but...

00:20:31.130 --> 00:20:33.920
Unless you ask me properly,
I must decline.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:44.180
May I... have this dance?

00:20:46.520 --> 00:20:47.850
I'd be delighted.

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:07.500
Aren't you a little too close?
Be careful not to touch me.

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:12.880
I'm used to it. It's just...
I haven't danced much at all.

00:21:12.880 --> 00:21:15.130
Neither have I.

00:21:15.130 --> 00:21:17.920
It's more difficult than I imagined.

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:22.890
But... it's delightful.

00:23:18.040 --> 00:23:21.090
Alice, can I ask you something?

00:23:21.090 --> 00:23:22.260
Certainly.

00:23:22.260 --> 00:23:25.760
What do you think of me?

00:23:25.760 --> 00:23:27.090
You're an important person.

00:23:27.090 --> 00:23:30.600
No, not in the sense of
a master and his servant...

00:23:30.600 --> 00:23:34.980
I'm asking you what you
think of me as a man.

00:23:34.980 --> 00:23:37.690
Well, of course I like you, Your Grace.

00:23:37.690 --> 00:23:38.900
Really?!

00:23:38.900 --> 00:23:39.770
Why, yes.

00:23:39.770 --> 00:23:44.190
I like you. I love you. I adore you. I
only have eyes for you, Your Grace.

00:23:44.190 --> 00:23:45.740
All right, that's enough!

00:23:45.740 --> 00:23:48.120
There aren't enough words
to express the way I feel.

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:52.200
I never would've thought you'd say that.

00:23:52.200 --> 00:23:54.330
I think I'll have my dinner now.

00:23:54.330 --> 00:23:56.710
Very well, Your Grace.

00:24:06.720 --> 00:24:09.890
"The Duke and the Meteor
Shower During the Full Moon."
